    <h1>Privacy &amp; your data</h1>
    <p class="lede">Short and plain, because there isn't much to hide: here's exactly what's collected when you join, why, and how to have it deleted.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="prose-section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose-block">

      <h2>Who's responsible for your data</h2>
      <p>The scottish new radicals is an informal, unincorporated network — no company, no legal entity, no treasurer. For data protection purposes, the network acts as the controller of the information you give us when you join. You can reach us at <a href="mailto:scottishnewradicals@gmail.com">scottishnewradicals@gmail.com</a> about anything on this page.</p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>Just two things, given voluntarily when you fill in the join form:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name</li>
        <li>Your email address</li>
      </ul>
      <p>When you later post us a stamped-addressed envelope to claim your membership card, we see the postal address on that envelope — but we don't type it into any system or keep a record of it. It's used once, to post your card back, and then discarded.</p>

      <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
      <p>To keep a registry of members and their numbers, and to send you the newsletter and any updates about the network. That's the whole purpose — your details are never used for anything else, and never sold or shared with advertisers.</p>

      <h2>Where it's held</h2>
      <p>Names and emails from the join form are stored in a Google Sheet, accessible only to the small team running the network. Newsletters are sent through Substack, which will process your email address as required to deliver them — Substack is a US-based company, so your email is processed outside the UK/EEA in order to receive updates. No other third party sees your details.</p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>For as long as you're part of the network, or until you ask us to remove you — whichever comes first. If you unsubscribe from the newsletter or ask to be taken off the registry, we'll delete your name and email from our records.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can ask us at any time to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>tell you what we hold about you</li>
        <li>correct anything that's wrong</li>
        <li>delete your details entirely</li>
        <li>withdraw your consent to us holding them</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Email <a href="mailto:scottishnewradicals@gmail.com">scottishnewradicals@gmail.com</a> and we'll action it. If you're ever unhappy with how we've handled a request, you also have the right to complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Information Commissioner's Office</a>.</p>

      <h2>Cookies &amp; tracking</h2>
      <p>This site doesn't use cookies, analytics, or any tracking scripts. Nothing about your visit is recorded beyond what you actively type into the join form.</p>

      <p class="prose-updated">Last updated: 2026</p>
    </div>
  </div>
